WEBVTT

00:00:02.920 --> 00:00:05.630
Manager Korone, we're here.

00:00:06.830 --> 00:00:08.110
Over here.

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:12.860
Ta-da!

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:19.390
It's your road racer, Maiharu Hiromi.

00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:21.870
What? Mine?

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:24.920
My road racer?

00:00:27.790 --> 00:00:30.510
It's very cool, Hiromi.

00:00:30.510 --> 00:00:31.340
Yeah.

00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:33.420
Manager, when did you build this?

00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:36.870
This is that frame from the race, isn't it?

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:41.470
Yeah. It's a well-balanced bike you 
can use in races or on long rides.

00:00:41.470 --> 00:00:43.230
This is amazing.

00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:45.600
It's a proper bicycle now.

00:00:46.950 --> 00:00:49.820
But where did you get the other parts?

00:00:49.820 --> 00:00:51.780
Yeah, about that...

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:56.300
Guys, we're building a high 
school girl's first bike.

00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:59.780
Could you bring me your leftover parts?

00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:02.290
Yeah!

00:01:03.290 --> 00:01:05.040
And that's how I made this.

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:06.290
I see.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:09.090
They're so nice.

00:01:09.090 --> 00:01:12.550
People who ride bikes switch 
out parts all the time.

00:01:12.550 --> 00:01:14.800
Sometimes they have previous parts leftover.

00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:18.030
It's easy to find enough for one 
bike when you pool your resources.

00:01:18.030 --> 00:01:22.520
H-How much will this cost?

00:01:22.520 --> 00:01:25.600
Since it was made from leftover parts,
you don't need to pay me.

00:01:28.060 --> 00:01:29.930
That's great, Hiromi.

00:01:30.670 --> 00:01:32.480
B-But...

00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:34.580
Are you sure I can have it?

00:01:34.580 --> 00:01:39.080
We all worked together to get this frame.

00:01:39.080 --> 00:01:42.000
Hiromi, you won this bike.

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:44.090
You stuck with it until the end and won.

00:01:44.090 --> 00:01:45.310
Don't worry about it.

00:01:45.310 --> 00:01:46.900
Yeah, yeah!

00:01:48.490 --> 00:01:51.180
The manager went to the
trouble of building it for you.

00:01:51.180 --> 00:01:52.980
You should accept it.

00:01:52.980 --> 00:01:54.390
There's no problem.

00:01:54.390 --> 00:01:56.140
Hiromi-san, use it.

00:01:56.140 --> 00:01:58.550
It's a present to you from us.

00:01:58.550 --> 00:02:00.440
Thanks, girls.

00:02:00.860 --> 00:02:03.070
I'll treasure my Unico forever.

00:02:03.070 --> 00:02:04.040
Unico?

00:02:04.040 --> 00:02:06.560
Yeah. Doesn't the light look like a horn?

00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:08.520
So I'll call it Unico.

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:11.280
That's nice. I call mine Momo.

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:13.510
What? Akizuki-san, you named your bike, too?

00:02:13.510 --> 00:02:14.320
Yeah.

00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:15.870
What a great idea.

00:02:15.870 --> 00:02:19.720
I'd like to name my road 
racer once I get mine.

00:02:19.720 --> 00:02:22.780
How does Super Miracle Shado #1 sound?

00:02:22.780 --> 00:02:24.620
"Shado"? You mean, like, "shadow"?

00:02:24.620 --> 00:02:26.930
That sounds like a name out of a comic book.

00:02:26.930 --> 00:02:30.330
No, "shado," the Japanese for "roadway"!

00:02:30.830 --> 00:02:34.000
Unico... My very own road racer.

00:04:04.090 --> 00:04:09.470
<b>#10  Let's Go On a Trip!</b>

00:04:05.800 --> 00:04:09.470
Looking toward the future, you have 
to decide what your club is doing next.

00:04:09.470 --> 00:04:12.320
Is there anything you want to do?

00:04:13.410 --> 00:04:16.840
All I want to do is go somewhere far away.

00:04:16.840 --> 00:04:19.650
Yes! I want to travel all across Japan.

00:04:19.650 --> 00:04:23.170
Me, too. I'd like to visit 
places I've never been before.

00:04:23.170 --> 00:04:25.800
Why don't you go on a trip, then?

00:04:26.450 --> 00:04:28.280
A trip?

00:04:28.280 --> 00:04:36.170
You can take your bikes on trains or 
planes and ride them at your destination.

00:04:36.170 --> 00:04:38.340
Since it involves riding other 
means of transportation,

00:04:38.340 --> 00:04:41.170
you can enjoy a much wider range of activities.

00:04:43.100 --> 00:04:45.280
Really? That's amazing.

00:04:45.280 --> 00:04:48.560
But can we take our bikes on trains?

00:04:48.560 --> 00:04:51.270
Naturally, you can't bring 
them on fully assembled.

00:04:51.840 --> 00:04:54.850
You'll have to break them down into a 
size designated by the railway company

00:04:54.850 --> 00:04:58.730
and put them in a special packing bag.

00:04:58.730 --> 00:05:01.230
Can we do that with our road racers?

00:05:01.230 --> 00:05:05.140
Yep. Since road bikes are so light, 
you could say they're good for trips.

00:05:05.140 --> 00:05:08.070
Then why don't we try that?

00:05:08.070 --> 00:05:11.870
You're right. Oh, but Sandy has a mommy bike.

00:05:12.210 --> 00:05:14.580
Oh, right. What should we do?

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:18.780
If you buy packing bags at my shop,
I'll rent you a road bike.

00:05:18.780 --> 00:05:20.340
What? Really?

00:05:20.340 --> 00:05:22.900
Hooray! We'll buy them immediately!

00:05:22.900 --> 00:05:25.050
But aren't they expensive?

00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:27.050
About that...

00:05:27.410 --> 00:05:31.380
Since you worked so hard at the criterium, 
our club got a little bit of money.

00:05:31.380 --> 00:05:35.390
You haven't been recognized as an official 
club yet, but an exception was made.

00:05:35.390 --> 00:05:36.700
What?

00:05:36.700 --> 00:05:37.900
Really?

00:05:37.900 --> 00:05:42.770
D-Do you think this is because we 
washed our money the other day?

00:05:43.410 --> 00:05:45.160
Maybe it is.

00:05:47.270 --> 00:05:49.700
Thank you.

00:05:51.020 --> 00:05:52.670
Come again.

00:05:52.670 --> 00:05:55.360
So these are packing bags, huh?

00:05:55.360 --> 00:05:57.610
Will they really fit in these?

00:05:57.610 --> 00:06:00.870
It'll be fine. I'll show you 
how to break down your bikes.

00:06:00.870 --> 00:06:02.640
Thank you.

00:06:05.820 --> 00:06:08.080
It took no time at all to break it down.

00:06:08.080 --> 00:06:09.590
That's amazing.

00:06:09.590 --> 00:06:13.350
Now you just put the bag over the parts.

00:06:17.060 --> 00:06:18.890
All done.

00:06:20.290 --> 00:06:23.160
Wow, it really fit.

00:06:23.160 --> 00:06:27.070
When you put your bikes together, 
just do the steps in reverse.

00:06:28.570 --> 00:06:31.570
Where should we go?

00:06:31.570 --> 00:06:34.000
Any recommendations?

00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:36.090
I want to ride all over Japan.

00:06:36.090 --> 00:06:41.580
Well, since it's our first trip,
I'd prefer to do a day trip.

00:06:41.710 --> 00:06:46.980
So a place that isn't too far 
that has a lot to see would be...

00:06:47.810 --> 00:06:49.170
the Miura Peninsula, I guess.

00:06:49.170 --> 00:06:50.340
The Miura Peninsula?

00:06:50.660 --> 00:06:55.200
Yeah. There's a naval port, 
fresh fish, and Miura radishes.

00:06:55.200 --> 00:06:58.180
I think it'd be a fun place to tour around.

00:06:58.180 --> 00:06:59.810
Wow...

00:07:00.140 --> 00:07:02.090
I'd like to go.

00:07:02.090 --> 00:07:06.530
In that case, why don't you start 
in Yokosuka and finish at Misaki?

00:07:06.530 --> 00:07:09.170
You should be able to ride 
that course in a day.

00:07:09.170 --> 00:07:10.580
It's decided.

00:07:10.580 --> 00:07:15.040
The Minami Kamakura Girls'
Bicycle Club's next destination is...

00:07:15.040 --> 00:07:17.490
The Miura Peninsula!

00:07:17.800 --> 00:07:20.500
<i>Really? You're going to the Miura Peninsula next?</i>

00:07:20.500 --> 00:07:24.180
It's nearby, but I haven't really 
been there, so I'm excited.

00:07:24.180 --> 00:07:27.050
<i>I'd like to go too, once I get out of the hospital.</i>

00:07:27.050 --> 00:07:29.330
<i>Fuyune, send me lots of pictures.</i>

00:07:29.330 --> 00:07:31.510
Sure. You can count on me.

00:07:32.200 --> 00:07:34.980
Nat-chan, you got a letter from your parents.

00:07:34.980 --> 00:07:36.820
Thanks, Auntie.

00:07:40.230 --> 00:07:42.690
<b>Doing well?
Great!
 From Dad and Mom
 P.S. You can do it!!</b>

00:07:43.730 --> 00:07:45.560
They're as terse as ever.

00:07:47.720 --> 00:07:50.700
I'd like to travel far away someday, too.

00:07:54.660 --> 00:07:57.830
Huh? Sis, you're polishing your bike again?

00:07:57.830 --> 00:08:02.010
Yeah. I'm going to be riding a lot tomorrow, 
so I thought I'd make it look nice.

00:08:02.580 --> 00:08:05.360
I see. Can I help?

00:08:05.360 --> 00:08:07.040
Yeah, thanks.

00:08:07.490 --> 00:08:11.420
Bicycles will take you anywhere.

00:08:11.420 --> 00:08:15.760
Across fields, over mountains, 
they travel along roads.

00:08:17.360 --> 00:08:19.800
Unico, we're going to ride a lot together.

00:08:20.690 --> 00:08:22.510
Hiromi, are you in there?

00:08:22.510 --> 00:08:22.810
What?

00:08:23.320 --> 00:08:28.150
I'm here to try a Japanese bath!

00:08:28.150 --> 00:08:30.030
What?

00:08:32.530 --> 00:08:34.180
What are you doing here?

00:08:34.180 --> 00:08:38.080
I just met your mother. She invited me in.

00:08:38.080 --> 00:08:39.490
What?

00:08:39.490 --> 00:08:42.330
Hiromi, let me wash your back.

00:08:42.330 --> 00:08:44.580
Y-You don't need to do that.

00:08:44.580 --> 00:08:50.690
Oh, no. Korone told me this 
is how Japanese people bathe.

00:08:50.690 --> 00:08:52.450
I've never heard that one before.

00:08:54.590 --> 00:08:55.720
Hiromi...

00:08:56.510 --> 00:08:59.010
Your swerves a little lacking.

00:08:59.010 --> 00:08:59.770
Lacking what?

00:08:59.770 --> 00:09:02.220
This area, around here.

00:09:02.220 --> 00:09:03.340
And this...

00:09:05.980 --> 00:09:07.920
Th-Those are called curves!

00:09:07.920 --> 00:09:10.950
No, wait! Stop staring! 
You're embarrassing me!

00:09:10.950 --> 00:09:13.010
No, no! There's no need to be shy!

00:09:13.010 --> 00:09:14.630
This is part of naked bonding!

00:09:14.630 --> 00:09:18.030
I'll wash your front next!

00:09:26.830 --> 00:09:33.200
I can't wait to go to the Miura Peninsula.

00:09:38.240 --> 00:09:40.640
Good morning, everyone.

00:09:40.640 --> 00:09:42.110
Good morning, Hiromi.

00:09:42.110 --> 00:09:43.340
Good morning.

00:09:43.340 --> 00:09:45.010
Good morning.

00:09:45.010 --> 00:09:47.230
Sensei, everyone's here.

00:09:47.230 --> 00:09:49.480
Then, let's go.

00:09:50.000 --> 00:09:55.720
While we're riding the train, our bikes 
will get in the way of other passengers,

00:09:55.720 --> 00:09:58.180
so let's try to ride in separate cars.

00:09:58.180 --> 00:09:59.980
Move to the edges once you get on.

00:09:59.980 --> 00:10:01.160
Okay.

00:10:07.550 --> 00:10:08.790
There.

00:10:17.970 --> 00:10:21.760
<i>Next stop, Yokosuka. Yokosuka.</i>

00:10:21.760 --> 00:10:23.650
We're almost there.

00:10:34.900 --> 00:10:38.070
We're here!

00:10:38.070 --> 00:10:40.750
That didn't take long at all.

00:10:40.750 --> 00:10:45.030
I saw a bunch of cool boats from the train.

00:10:45.030 --> 00:10:46.340
Are they over there?

00:10:46.340 --> 00:10:47.880
Oh, I'd like to see them!

00:10:47.880 --> 00:10:48.730
Let's go!

00:10:48.730 --> 00:10:50.290
Don't rush.

00:10:50.650 --> 00:10:53.660
Sensei, should we reassemble our bikes now?

00:10:53.660 --> 00:10:57.300
Well, we'd get in the way here.

00:10:57.300 --> 00:10:58.770
Why don't we go to a park?

00:10:58.770 --> 00:11:00.840
All right!

00:11:03.630 --> 00:11:05.260
Amazing.

00:11:05.260 --> 00:11:07.310
They're so cool.

00:11:07.310 --> 00:11:09.880
There are some American ships over there.

00:11:09.880 --> 00:11:12.350
Oh, really?

00:11:13.270 --> 00:11:14.860
There.

00:11:14.860 --> 00:11:16.390
That should do it.

00:11:16.390 --> 00:11:18.990
Make sure you check everything carefully.

00:11:19.780 --> 00:11:21.150
It's not wobbling.

00:11:21.150 --> 00:11:23.280
I'm good, too.

00:11:23.280 --> 00:11:27.160
Everyone, look this way.

00:11:30.240 --> 00:11:32.110
What do you think?

00:11:32.110 --> 00:11:34.350
You look great, Sandy.

00:11:34.350 --> 00:11:36.520
When did you get your uniform made?

00:11:36.520 --> 00:11:39.090
Tomoe let me borrow one.

00:11:39.090 --> 00:11:41.710
Yuika made a spare.

00:11:41.710 --> 00:11:45.300
Really? That's great, Sandy.

00:11:45.300 --> 00:11:46.810
Yeah.

00:11:46.810 --> 00:11:49.220
Sensei, we're ready.

00:11:49.220 --> 00:11:50.930
Let's go.

00:11:50.930 --> 00:11:52.520
Does anyone need to use the bathroom?

00:11:53.200 --> 00:11:54.660
I think I'm okay.

00:11:54.660 --> 00:11:55.570
Me, too.

00:11:58.970 --> 00:12:02.000
Let me tell you something about touring.

00:12:02.000 --> 00:12:04.280
First, always go to the 
bathroom when you can.

00:12:05.400 --> 00:12:08.970
If you suddenly need to go, there's no 
guarantee you'll be able to right away.

00:12:08.970 --> 00:12:12.770
You maybe be able to in urban areas,
but if you're in the mountains or by the sea,

00:12:12.770 --> 00:12:14.830
you may not be able to find 
a bathroom immediately.

00:12:14.830 --> 00:12:16.250
You're right.

00:12:16.250 --> 00:12:17.750
And one more thing.

00:12:18.130 --> 00:12:22.220
Buy as much fluid as you can, when you can.

00:12:22.220 --> 00:12:26.480
Like bathrooms, you can't always 
get more when you need it.

00:12:26.480 --> 00:12:29.340
There aren't any shops 
in uninhabited mountains,

00:12:29.340 --> 00:12:31.180
and vending machines are sometimes broken.

00:12:31.580 --> 00:12:34.640
It's important to always keep enough 
on you so you can drink anytime.

00:12:38.610 --> 00:12:40.220
A-Actually...

00:12:40.220 --> 00:12:41.600
I'm going to the bathroom.

00:12:41.600 --> 00:12:42.720
Me, too.

00:12:42.720 --> 00:12:44.370
I'll go buy some drinks.

00:12:44.370 --> 00:12:45.380
Let's go together.

00:12:46.240 --> 00:12:49.990
Now we're ready to start 
our Miura Peninsula tour.

00:12:49.990 --> 00:12:51.190
Yeah!

00:13:00.110 --> 00:13:01.760
We're riding through the city.

00:13:19.550 --> 00:13:21.480
It's like a tropical paradise.

00:13:26.450 --> 00:13:29.240
I know. Why don't we try forming a train?

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:32.560
Like we did during the criterium?

00:13:32.560 --> 00:13:35.320
Yeah. It's a good opportunity to review.

00:13:42.130 --> 00:13:44.200
Looking good.

00:13:44.200 --> 00:13:46.760
We'll take turns leading 
the group as we ride along.

00:13:46.760 --> 00:13:47.670
Okay.

00:14:05.990 --> 00:14:07.980
We did it, girls.

00:14:07.980 --> 00:14:10.520
Yeah, I think we managed okay.

00:14:10.520 --> 00:14:12.040
What are you talking about?

00:14:12.040 --> 00:14:14.870
It was really tough while 
Sandy was the leader.

00:14:15.180 --> 00:14:17.800
She kept riding forward without 
any consideration for the train.

00:14:17.800 --> 00:14:21.130
You're just too weak.

00:14:21.670 --> 00:14:23.800
No, you ride too fast.

00:14:23.800 --> 00:14:26.380
Okay, okay. Let's practice again.

00:14:26.380 --> 00:14:30.260
Anyway, look. That's where we started.

00:14:30.260 --> 00:14:32.170
What? It's so far away.

00:14:32.170 --> 00:14:36.100
How surprising! I can't 
believe we've come so far.

00:14:36.100 --> 00:14:39.060
We made it this far in the blink of an eye.

00:14:39.060 --> 00:14:42.230
Road racers really are amazing.

00:14:45.290 --> 00:14:47.730
Touring is fun, isn't it?

00:14:47.730 --> 00:14:49.360
Right? Right? Right? Right?

00:14:49.360 --> 00:14:52.310
How long did it take to get here?

00:14:52.310 --> 00:14:54.330
Don't worry about that too much.

00:14:54.670 --> 00:14:58.890
Forgetting the time and taking it 
easy is what makes touring fun.

00:14:59.790 --> 00:15:00.930
You're right.

00:15:02.150 --> 00:15:04.040
Hey, I can see Mt. Fuji.

00:15:04.040 --> 00:15:05.350
What? Where?

00:15:05.350 --> 00:15:06.650
Look.

00:15:06.650 --> 00:15:08.190
You're right.

00:15:08.190 --> 00:15:10.640
It looks smaller than it does from Kamakura.

00:15:10.640 --> 00:15:13.360
But Mt. Fuji is beautiful, large or small.

00:15:14.750 --> 00:15:17.600
I'd like to climb Mt. Fuji someday.

00:15:17.600 --> 00:15:18.840
That's a good idea.

00:15:18.840 --> 00:15:21.310
We can ride our bikes 
up to the fifth station.

00:15:21.310 --> 00:15:25.230
It might be fun to ride there 
and hike the rest of the way up.

00:15:26.270 --> 00:15:28.780
I'm going to run out of energy this time.

00:15:28.780 --> 00:15:31.430
Let's do it together, Fuyune-san.

00:15:31.430 --> 00:15:34.620
What? If only I could.

00:15:34.620 --> 00:15:36.500
What kind of answer is that?

00:15:40.000 --> 00:15:42.790
Going downhill is easy.

00:15:43.480 --> 00:15:45.850
See you there, girls.

00:15:46.520 --> 00:15:48.840
Fuyune-san, wait!

00:15:48.840 --> 00:15:50.730
What?

00:15:51.780 --> 00:15:53.590
Don't go any faster.

00:15:53.590 --> 00:15:56.890
Your speed increases while you're going 
downhill, and it can be dangerous.

00:15:56.890 --> 00:15:57.810
The rest of you, too.

00:15:58.460 --> 00:16:02.110
You'll go faster than you think on downhills.

00:16:02.110 --> 00:16:06.190
If you fall going at that speed,
you could seriously injure yourself.

00:16:07.980 --> 00:16:09.570
We'll be careful!

00:16:11.780 --> 00:16:13.480
It's a tunnel.

00:16:14.280 --> 00:16:17.740
Since it's narrow inside tunnels 
and you ride close to cars,

00:16:17.740 --> 00:16:19.450
I don't like them much.

00:16:19.450 --> 00:16:21.290
They're loud and echoey, too.

00:16:21.290 --> 00:16:23.200
You're right.

00:16:23.200 --> 00:16:24.890
Let's get through it quickly.

00:16:24.890 --> 00:16:25.880
Yeah!

00:16:31.030 --> 00:16:33.800
<b>Kannonsaki Public Park
 Observation Area</b>

00:16:34.490 --> 00:16:36.970
Th-The tunnel was scary.

00:16:36.970 --> 00:16:38.070
Yeah.

00:16:38.070 --> 00:16:40.390
I thought I was going to get run over.

00:16:43.260 --> 00:16:45.010
It's sweet.

00:16:45.010 --> 00:16:46.770
It's good, isn't it?

00:16:46.770 --> 00:16:48.480
What kind of tea is this?

00:16:48.480 --> 00:16:53.540
It's called sherpa tea. It's a sweet 
black tea made with wild grapes.

00:16:53.540 --> 00:16:56.040
It's drunk by sherpas who 
help people climb mountains.

00:16:56.040 --> 00:16:57.990
It's supposed to re-energize you.

00:16:57.990 --> 00:17:01.190
Really? You know a lot about tea.

00:17:01.190 --> 00:17:04.710
Daddy and I used to drink it all 
the time when we went hiking.

00:17:04.710 --> 00:17:07.700
Sandy-san, you're great at all 
kinds of outdoor activities.

00:17:07.700 --> 00:17:09.880
No wonder you have so much stamina.

00:17:11.040 --> 00:17:15.830
Unlike the ocean we see in Kamakura, 
we can see the opposite coast.

00:17:17.010 --> 00:17:18.860
Is that Chiba Prefecture?

00:17:18.860 --> 00:17:21.350
Yeah, it's the Boso Peninsula.

00:17:21.350 --> 00:17:24.430
There are people living over there, too.

00:17:24.430 --> 00:17:25.880
Of course.

00:17:28.510 --> 00:17:31.280
I'd like to go there someday.

00:17:32.630 --> 00:17:36.090
And even farther away.

00:17:36.550 --> 00:17:37.650
Yeah.

00:17:37.650 --> 00:17:39.380
I'd like to go, too.

00:17:48.140 --> 00:17:49.590
They fell asleep.

00:17:50.420 --> 00:17:52.010
So did Fuyune-san.

00:17:52.010 --> 00:17:54.380
We did wake up early this morning.

00:17:54.380 --> 00:17:57.300
I can't believe they can sleep out here.

00:17:59.260 --> 00:18:01.260
Well, it can't be helped.

00:18:01.260 --> 00:18:03.050
Let's wait until they wake up.

00:18:03.050 --> 00:18:03.690
Yeah.

00:18:08.020 --> 00:18:09.690
Good morning, Fuyune-san.

00:18:09.690 --> 00:18:12.260
Huh? How long was I asleep?

00:18:12.260 --> 00:18:13.700
About ten minutes.

00:18:13.700 --> 00:18:17.150
What? I feel like I slept 
a lot longer than that.

00:18:18.080 --> 00:18:20.680
Has the sun risen higher?

00:18:20.680 --> 00:18:22.920
It's starting to get pretty warm.

00:18:22.920 --> 00:18:24.720
It's perfect for touring.

00:18:27.660 --> 00:18:28.950
They're up, too.

00:18:28.950 --> 00:18:31.790
Tomo-chan, I'm hungry.

00:18:31.790 --> 00:18:34.910
What? Did you eat breakfast?

00:18:34.910 --> 00:18:37.160
I had some yogurt.

00:18:37.160 --> 00:18:38.860
I thought I was going to be late.

00:18:38.860 --> 00:18:40.180
That's no good.

00:18:40.180 --> 00:18:43.260
Huh? Sensei's not here.

00:18:43.260 --> 00:18:45.310
Did she go to the bathroom?

00:18:45.310 --> 00:18:47.020
Oh, actually...

00:18:47.990 --> 00:18:48.950
What?

00:18:48.950 --> 00:18:51.520
You'll wake them.

00:18:51.520 --> 00:18:56.110
B-But we can't go to Misaki without you.

00:18:56.110 --> 00:18:58.380
It's impossible.

00:18:58.380 --> 00:19:02.410
But it's no fun if I pull 
the whole way, right?

00:19:02.410 --> 00:19:05.150
This is your club activity.

00:19:05.150 --> 00:19:09.120
Don't you think getting lost 
together will be a good experience?

00:19:09.900 --> 00:19:12.770
B-But... right?

00:19:12.770 --> 00:19:13.380
Yeah.

00:19:13.380 --> 00:19:18.450
Well, if you really get stuck, call me.

00:19:18.450 --> 00:19:20.060
I'll be right there.

00:19:21.130 --> 00:19:23.560
So she left us.

00:19:23.560 --> 00:19:24.890
What?

00:19:25.950 --> 00:19:28.850
Will we be okay?

00:19:31.170 --> 00:19:32.690
Let's go, girls.

00:19:32.690 --> 00:19:33.390
What?

00:19:33.390 --> 00:19:35.170
We made it this far.

00:19:35.170 --> 00:19:36.390
All we can do is move forward.

00:19:36.390 --> 00:19:38.650
Bicycles can't go in reverse, right?

00:19:39.880 --> 00:19:40.560
What?

00:19:47.000 --> 00:19:48.710
Oh, Hiromi.

00:19:51.250 --> 00:19:52.740
Shall we go?

00:19:52.740 --> 00:19:54.420
Let's ride to Misaki.

00:19:54.420 --> 00:19:55.820
Let's do this.

00:19:55.820 --> 00:19:58.180
Let's head for the finish line.

00:19:58.180 --> 00:20:00.010
Yeah, together.

00:20:00.320 --> 00:20:02.100
Yeah!

00:21:36.150 --> 00:21:40.200
<i>The appeal of road bikes on full display 
makes you want to start riding tomorrow.</i>

00:21:40.200 --> 00:21:43.250
<i>A-O-P: The first cycling club.</i>

00:21:44.070 --> 00:21:49.990
<b>Kamakura Cycling</b>

00:21:44.070 --> 00:21:49.990
<b>Enoshima</b>

00:21:44.070 --> 00:21:49.990
<b>Shichirigahama</b>

00:21:44.070 --> 00:21:49.990
<b>Inamuragasaki</b>

00:21:44.070 --> 00:21:49.990
<b>Enoshima Line</b>

00:21:44.070 --> 00:21:49.990
<b>Kamakura Station</b>

00:21:44.070 --> 00:21:49.990
<b>Yokosuka Line</b>

00:21:44.780 --> 00:21:47.380
<i>We're heading for Enoshima while 
making stops along the way</i>

00:21:47.380 --> 00:21:49.990
<i>in our first cycling tour of Kamakura.</i>

00:21:50.550 --> 00:21:55.420
<i>Last time we departed from Kamakura 
Station and enjoyed the Kotoku-in Temple.</i>

00:21:55.420 --> 00:21:56.860
<i>Our next destination is...</i>

00:21:57.590 --> 00:21:59.930
It's a terrace with the view of the ocean

00:21:59.930 --> 00:22:03.000
where you can eat sweets 
from a really stylish café.

00:22:01.520 --> 00:22:03.360
I really want sweets! I want some of that.

00:22:03.360 --> 00:22:03.950
Want to go?

00:22:03.690 --> 00:22:08.630
<b>Sweets on a terrace with a view of the ocean!</b>

00:22:03.950 --> 00:22:08.630
<i>Our destination this time is a 
stylish cafe that serves sweets.</i>

00:22:09.240 --> 00:22:12.640
<i>It's time to go.</i>

00:22:12.640 --> 00:22:17.640
Kamakura Cycling

00:22:12.640 --> 00:22:17.640
<b>Shichirigahama</b>

00:22:12.640 --> 00:22:17.640
<b>Inamuragasaki</b>

00:22:12.640 --> 00:22:17.640
<b>Enoshima Line</b>

00:22:12.640 --> 00:22:17.640
<b>Yokosuka Line</b>

00:22:13.170 --> 00:22:17.050
<i>We'll be riding along the 
coast towards Shichirigahama.</i>

00:22:17.640 --> 00:22:21.750
* Filmed on bicycle and pedestrian path

00:22:19.810 --> 00:22:21.400
It's the ocean.

00:22:21.840 --> 00:22:23.290
Wow.

00:22:24.100 --> 00:22:27.650
This place is called Inamuragasaki.

00:22:24.300 --> 00:22:28.110
<b>Inamuragasaki</b>

00:22:27.650 --> 00:22:29.680
Enoshima is that way.

00:22:29.680 --> 00:22:32.730
It's Enoshima. I can see Enoshima.

00:22:34.450 --> 00:22:38.710
<i>If the weather's good enough, 
you can even see Mt. Fuji clearly.</i>

00:22:38.730 --> 00:22:41.440
Let's make a stop here.

00:22:41.440 --> 00:22:42.150
Okay.

00:22:42.150 --> 00:22:43.260
Long time, no see.

00:22:44.110 --> 00:22:45.260
There.

00:22:45.260 --> 00:22:50.500
<i>Make a turn at the Yukiaibashi signal,
and the store we're headed to is right there.</i>

00:22:51.960 --> 00:22:53.290
Drum roll, please.

00:22:53.290 --> 00:22:53.870
We're here?

00:22:53.870 --> 00:22:54.900
This is it!

00:22:56.590 --> 00:22:57.720
How stylish.

00:22:57.720 --> 00:22:58.290
Isn't it?

00:22:58.290 --> 00:22:59.510
Yeah, it's wonderful.

00:22:59.510 --> 00:23:00.270
Yeah.

00:23:00.590 --> 00:23:05.310
<i>This is the Amalfi Caffe,
the shop I just had to visit.</i>

00:23:05.310 --> 00:23:10.280
<i>It makes you feel like you're 
at Italy's Amalfi Coast.</i>

00:23:11.660 --> 00:23:22.250
<b>Delizie al limone
 ¥1000 with drink (includes tax)
 *As of February 2017</b>

00:23:12.110 --> 00:23:14.750
<i>Their sweets are great, too.</i>

00:23:14.750 --> 00:23:16.160
<i>Their most popular dish</i>

00:23:16.160 --> 00:23:19.900
<i>is a traditional sweet served with 
refreshing lemon-flavored cream,</i>

00:23:19.900 --> 00:23:21.470
<i>the delizie al limone.</i>

00:23:22.250 --> 00:23:24.740
After tiring my body out riding a bike,

00:23:24.740 --> 00:23:27.130
it feels great to fill it 
with something sweet.

00:23:27.130 --> 00:23:28.050
Yeah.

00:23:28.510 --> 00:23:31.290
<i>Why don't you stop by?</i>

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:40.020
<b>Next Time
 "Bicycles Are Strange"</b>
